<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="createorgrobotfederation">
  <title>createOrgRobotFederation</title>
  <shortdesc>Create a federation configuration for the specified organization robot.</shortdesc>
  <refbody>
    <section id="createorgrobotfederation-post">
      <title>POST /api/v1/organization/{orgname}/robots/{robot_shortname}/federation</title>
      <p>Create or replace the federation configuration for the specified organization robot.</p>
      <p><b>Authorizations: </b>oauth2_implicit (<b>user:admin</b>)</p>
    </section>
    <section id="createorgrobotfederation-path-parameters">
      <title>Path parameters</title>
      <table>
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <colspec colname="col_1" colwidth="*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_2" colwidth="*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_3" colwidth="*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_4" colwidth="*"/>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry>Type</entry>
              <entry>Name</entry>
              <entry>Description</entry>
              <entry>Schema</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>path</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p><b>orgname</b> + <b>robot_shortname</b><i>required</i></p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>The name of the organization and the short name for the robot, without any user or organization prefix</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>string</p>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section id="createorgrobotfederation-request-body-schema">
      <title>Request body schema (application/json)</title>
      <p>Array of federation configuration entries for the robot.</p>
      <note type="important">
        <p>In Red Hat Quay 3.18, create and update requests persist <codeph>issuer</codeph> and <codeph>subject</codeph> only. The optional <codeph>audiences</codeph> field is not stored from API requests, and the Red Hat Quay v2 UI federation modal does not provide an <codeph>audiences</codeph> field. When <codeph>audiences</codeph> is present in stored federation configuration, Red Hat Quay validates the token audience during federated robot token exchange. When it is absent, audience validation is skipped and Red Hat Quay logs a deprecation warning.</p>
      </note>
      <table>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="col_1" colwidth="*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_2" colwidth="*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_3" colwidth="*"/>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry>Name</entry>
              <entry>Description</entry>
              <entry>Schema</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>
                  <b>issuer</b>
                </p>
                <p>
                  <i>required</i>
                </p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>Issuer URL of the external OIDC provider for this federation entry</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>string</p>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>
                  <b>subject</b>
                </p>
                <p>
                  <i>required</i>
                </p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>Subject (<codeph>sub</codeph> claim) of the external OIDC identity authorized for this robot</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>string</p>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>
                  <b>audiences</b>
                </p>
                <p>
                  <i>optional</i>
                </p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>List of acceptable token audience (<codeph>aud</codeph> claim) values for this federation entry. Reserved for future API support; not persisted by create or update requests in Red Hat Quay 3.18.</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>array of strings</p>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <p outputclass="title">
        <b>Example request body</b>
      </p>
      <codeblock outputclass="language-json">[
  {
    "issuer": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/&lt;tenant-id&gt;/v2.0",
    "subject": "&lt;user-object-id&gt;"
  }
]</codeblock>
    </section>
